    "reason": "The PR (rust-lang/rust#119672) is explicitly a pass-ordering/efficiency change: it sandwiches optimizations between two DeadStoreElimination runs, moves CopyProp to the end, and removes simplify_locals from DSE because the full SimplifyLocals pass runs shortly after. The frozen analysis itself states that the old ordering did not miscompile programs and that both variants are semantically valid. The decoded MIR layers support this: the only differences are pass names (`DeadStoreElimination` vs `-initial`/`-final`), where copies/moves are rewritten, and where simplification occurs; there is no source-level value-semantics change to encode as an \"incorrect transformation.\" In particular, DSE-final only converts a copy to a move when the source is dead (e.g. `use_both(_1, move _1)` for a Copy i32 is still semantically a copy), and it deliberately preserves packed-struct copies and PlaceMention/provenance uses. Therefore any original/transformed Rust function pair that differs in observable numeric/boolean/character output would be a fabricated unrelated rewrite rather than the historical change, so no source-grounded semantic counterexample can be validated with test_program_pair.",
