    "incorrectTransformation": "The historically superseded pipeline (the transformation being changed here) was: early CopyProp before GVN; a single late DSE; no CopyProp followed by DSE at the end. The PR replaces it with DSE::Initial before GVN, GVN before SeparateConstSwitch, and CopyProp immediately followed by DSE::Final at the end of the pipeline. This is explicitly an efficiency/reordering change, not a claim that the old ordering miscompiled programs: the PR says \"This PR reorders MIR optimization passes in an attempt to increase their efficiency.\" A comparison harness should vary only this pass ordering (or the presence/absence of DSE::Final after CopyProp), holding the input program fixed, and compare resulting MIR dumps; both variants are semantically valid.",
    "inputDomain": "Optimized MIR of Rust functions under mir_opt_level >= 2, containing local-to-local copies and moves that may later be overwritten, repeated call arguments, packed-struct field reads, loops/assignment cycles, PlaceMention statements, and provenance-sensitive operations (pointer-to-int casts and retags).",
    "kind": "optimization",
    "originalLogic": "Before this PR, the optimized-MIR pipeline ran CopyProp early (immediately after SimplifyLocals::BeforeConstProp and before SeparateConstSwitch/GVN), ran DSE only once later (after SimplifyComparisonIntegral and before DestinationPropagation), and DSE's eliminate() ended by calling crate::simplify::simplify_locals(body, tcx). The old ordering as shown by the diff was: SimplifyLocals::BeforeConstProp, CopyProp, SeparateConstSwitch, GVN, SimplifyLocals::AfterGVN, DataflowConstProp, ..., DeadStoreElimination, DestinationPropagation, ..., SimplifyCfg::Final, RenameReturnPlace.",
