    "pitfalls": [
      "Do not conflate the two independent reasons a copy stays a copy: (a) borrowing/move restrictions such as a field of a packed struct, and (b) the source being live/overwritten by a later assignment. The packed-struct test asserts a copy remains a copy after DSE-final; the cycle test asserts stores are not removed because of loops/pending stores.",
      "DSE-final must not convert a copy into a move when the place is not movable, e.g. a packed-struct field: the test comment says \"We have a packed struct, verify that the copy is not turned into a move.\" and checks `use_both(const 0_i32, (_1.1: i32))`.",
      "For repeated arguments, DSE-final may change the second use of the same local to a move, e.g. `use_both(_1, move _1)` for `use_both(x, x)`; this is an ordering-sensitive transformation, not a general license to move every copy.",
      "Cycle/loop handling: with non-transitive liveness, stores in an assignment cycle may look dead but must be preserved; DSE-initial is expected to leave no assignments satisfying `CHECK-NOT: {{_.*}} = {{_.*}};` / `CHECK-NOT: {{_.*}} = move {{_.*}};` only for that specially constructed cycle.",
      "PlaceMention is a use of the destructured place and must not be treated as a dead store; DSE-initial must preserve `PlaceMention([[tmp:_.*]])`.",
      "Provenance-sensitive operations must count as uses: DSE must not remove PointerExposeAddress casts (`as usize (PointerExposeAddress)`) or Retag statements (`Retag([fn entry] _1);`).",
      "Because simplify_locals was removed from DSE, a standalone DSE unit test sees unsimplified locals; do not attribute those simplifications to DSE, and remember the full SimplifyLocals pass runs shortly after.",
      "Pass names matter for test harnesses: the single old DeadStoreElimination dump was split into DeadStoreElimination-initial and DeadStoreElimination-final, so EMIT_MIR/unit-test annotations must target the correct variant."
